I was able to reproduce this issue.

The following (new) uint test in `topology_manager_tests.go` fails unexpectedly:
```
        {
            name: "Two providers, one with no preference",
            policy: NewSingleNumaNodePolicy(),
            hp: []HintProvider{
                &mockHintProvider{
                    map[string][]TopologyHint{
                        "resource1": {
                            {
                                NUMANodeAffinity: NewTestBitMask(0),
                                Preferred:        true,
                            },
                            {
                                NUMANodeAffinity: NewTestBitMask(1),
                                Preferred:        true,
                            },
                            {
                                NUMANodeAffinity: NewTestBitMask(0,1),
                                Preferred:        false,
                            },
                        },
                    },
                },
                &mockHintProvider{
                    map[string][]TopologyHint{
                        "resource2": {
                            {
                                NUMANodeAffinity: NewTestBitMask(0,1),
                                Preferred:        true,
                            },
                        },
                    },
                },
            },
            expected: TopologyHint{
                NUMANodeAffinity: NewTestBitMask(0),
                Preferred:        true,
            },
        },
```

With any policy other than the `SingleNumaNodePolicy()` this test passes.

This is due to 3 factors:
1) The CPUManager is the only hint provider passing actual valid hints `[{01 true}, {10 true}, {11 false}]`

2) The devicemanager passes `nil` back as its hints, resulting in a single `{11 true}` (i.e. don’t care) hint

3) We added a special casing for the `SingleNumaNodePolicy()` in the device manager that essentially turns the devicemanager's hint into a `{11 false}`: https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/master/pkg/kubelet/cm/topologymanager/topology_manager.go#L243

Because the single hint from the devicemanager now has a `false` preference, there is no chance to have it combine with any of the CPUManager hints to result in a successful hint.

This should ultimately be addressed as part of the following in 1.17 
https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/83478

But we should put a one-off patch into the 1.16.x branch to fix this in 1.16.
